  ('03492124-f98c-4af0-8d73-4324fa2a22af','Anchorage''s Northwest Archers Association Inc runs as a volunteer club rather than a storefront business, which is common for archery groups in South Central Alaska, where organized shooting often depends on member turnout and seasonal daylight more than posted hours. Alaska''s hunting culture runs deep, and a member-driven association in the state''s largest city likely draws both target archers and bowhunters keeping their form sharp between seasons. There''s no public detail here on course layout, indoor versus outdoor shooting, or membership requirements, so this listing reads as a starting point rather than a full picture. Anyone curious about joining or visiting should reach out to the association directly to confirm current activity and how to get involved.'),
  ('67d46c3e-d0d9-47bd-b67a-33a6d77d9c7c','Tucked into Colebrook in Connecticut''s rural northwest corner, the Northwest Connecticut Sportsman''s Association operates as a club rather than a commercial range, the kind of setup built around dues-paying members instead of walk-in traffic. That part of Litchfield County is heavily wooded and popular with hunters, so a sportsman''s association here likely covers archery alongside other outdoor pursuits rather than existing as a single-purpose archery facility. No specifics are listed on lanes, 3D courses, or lesson programs, which is typical for member clubs that don''t advertise widely beyond their own roster. Interested archers should contact the association directly to ask about membership, guest access, and what shooting options are actually available on site.'),
  ('f5f84419-ea8f-407b-b313-aa284602975c','The Northwoods Archery Club, based near Roscommon in Michigan''s north-central Lower Peninsula, is a volunteer-run outfit in country better known for deer camps than city archery ranges. Roscommon sits in the heart of Michigan''s northern woods, an area where volunteer clubs often exist to give local bowhunters a place to shoot year-round rather than to run a commercial operation. Nothing here is listed about course type, hours, or amenities, which lines up with how a lot of these grassroots northern Michigan clubs operate on word of mouth. Anyone wanting to shoot there or learn more about membership should get in touch with the club directly before planning a visit.'),
  ('2ed7728d-95c0-409f-9ed3-10f9e53e9be6','Northwoods Bowmens Club, Inc. serves the Novato area north of San Francisco as a volunteer-run club that includes lessons among its offerings, a notable feature for archers in Marin County who want structured instruction rather than just a place to shoot on their own. Being volunteer-organized rather than a commercial business, the club likely relies on member involvement to keep programs like lessons running, which is common for Northern California archery groups outside the big commercial ranges of the Bay Area. Details on course layout, 3D shooting, or membership dues aren''t listed publicly, so anyone interested in the lesson program should reach out directly to confirm scheduling, cost, and availability.'),
  ('b78e1fce-15e8-4455-ba17-0d5339953cab','Obissquasoit Bowmen, based in Bridgeton in South Jersey, is a volunteer club running both a 3D course and a field course across twelve lanes, a combination that lets members practice realistic animal-target shooting alongside the longer-range, varied-terrain discipline of field archery in one location. South Jersey''s mix of farmland and wooded tracts makes it well suited to that kind of layout, and having both course types under one volunteer-run club is more than a lot of small regional groups offer. The twelve lanes suggest a reasonably sized property built for group shoots rather than a single backyard setup. Anyone interested in shooting either course or joining as a member should contact the club directly for access and scheduling.'),
  ('61e80f35-f4b8-4e82-910a-b80b433c5c5d','Oceana Archers is a volunteer club based in Hart, a small community along Michigan''s western Lake Michigan shoreline in Oceana County, fitting country better known for orchards and hunting land than commercial archery ranges. A club like this in rural west Michigan likely serves local bowhunters and recreational shooters through member-organized shoots rather than posted business hours. No details are listed here about course type, amenities, or membership requirements, which is typical for small-town volunteer clubs that don''t maintain much of a public presence beyond their name and location. Anyone interested in getting involved should contact Oceana Archers directly to find out about meeting times, guest policy, and how to join.'),
  ('ddc9cfd1-2bf5-4664-b314-926486e0eae0','Odd Vane Out Archery operates as a commercial business in Chelsea, a small town in northeastern Oklahoma along the Route 66 corridor. Commercial archery operations in this part of the state tend to serve a mix of recreational shooters and bowhunters tuning up ahead of deer season, though nothing specific is listed here about lanes, a pro shop, or lesson offerings for this particular location. Northeastern Oklahoma has a solid rural hunting culture, and a named commercial range in a town the size of Chelsea likely functions as a local gathering spot for archers rather than a large destination facility. Anyone interested in shooting there should call ahead to confirm hours, pricing, and what services are currently available.'),
  ('68afc88f-ed5e-4aa0-84e7-d1b7fc8654b7','OE Archers in Tipp City, just north of Dayton, is a volunteer club that includes a pro shop and runs across twenty-seven lanes, a sizable setup for a member-organized operation rather than a commercial storefront. Having an on-site pro shop alongside that many lanes suggests a club built to handle a real membership base and probably league or tournament-style shooting rather than a handful of casual members. The Dayton area has a decent concentration of archery activity, and a volunteer club with this kind of infrastructure likely draws archers from beyond Tipp City itself. Membership terms, hours, and course type aren''t listed here, so anyone interested should contact OE Archers directly to learn how to join or visit.'),
  ('fd028f26-d90b-4d17-8773-b90b2283b9a9','The Ogemaw Hills Sportsmen Association is a volunteer club based in West Branch, in north-central Michigan''s Ogemaw County, an area shaped by state forest land and a strong deer hunting tradition. A sportsmen''s association in this part of the state often covers archery as one piece of a broader outdoor recreation mission rather than running purely as a dedicated archery range. No specific detail is listed here about course layout, lesson programs, or amenities, which tracks with how many rural Michigan sportsmen''s clubs operate primarily for their own membership rather than the general public. Anyone interested in archery access or joining should contact the association directly to confirm current opportunities and requirements.'),
  ('a1a50d6e-dbc2-4146-b847-362285197881','As its name suggests, the Ohio Archery Learning Center in Chesterland, east of Cleveland, is a commercial facility built around teaching, offering lessons across eight lanes rather than positioning itself as a pure walk-in range for already-experienced shooters. That combination of a manageable lane count with an explicit lesson program points to a business designed for beginners and families getting their first real instruction, which fits the northeast Ohio suburbs'' demand for accessible, structured programs. Details on pro shop services, course type, or additional amenities aren''t listed here. Anyone in the Chesterland or greater Cleveland area looking to start archery lessons should contact the center directly to check current class times and pricing.'),
  ('509ef5a2-16f9-4cd0-9158-719c76205c0d','Ohio Premier Archery and Sports, located in Middlefield in Geauga County, is a commercial facility that runs an actual 3D course, giving northeast Ohio archers and bowhunters a place to shoot realistic animal targets rather than only paper or bag targets. Geauga County''s rural, wooded character makes it a natural fit for a 3D layout, and a commercial business offering that format typically serves hunters tuning up for deer season alongside archers who enjoy the format year-round. No specifics are listed here about a pro shop, lessons, or additional lanes beyond the 3D course itself. Anyone interested in shooting the course should contact Ohio Premier Archery and Sports directly to confirm hours and pricing.')
